{
  "text": "This free Claude Code skill copies any animation you see online, frame by frame, and then proves the copy moves the same. It already has 2.4K stars on GitHub. It's called reanimate. Point it at a live site, a screen recording, a GIF or a Lottie file. It records the motion in a headless browser, writes a spec for every element, builds it in CSS, Framer Motion or GSAP, then films its own copy and measures the difference. On Vercel's toolbar it matched 417 of 417 frames. But don't stop at a copy. Ask it to clone this and add that, and build your own on top. Comment ANIMATE and I'll send you the link.",
